## Entry for the Table of Contents
A family of highly tunable MOFs are studied for their ability to form terminal metal-oxo species that can activate strong $C-H$ bonds. By changing the metal or bridging ligands, the stability and reactivity of the metal-oxo active sites can be drastically altered. For the Mn- and Fe-containing MOFs, a transition from ferromagnetic to antiferromagnetic coupling between the metal and terminal oxo ligand greatly reduces the barrier for $C-H$ activation.
